\section*{Generic maximal Seshadri constants in positive characteristic}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
The same eventual volume-bound equality for ordinary multipoint Seshadri constants is claimed in positive characteristic at geometric generic tuples, in dimensions two and higher. The cited manuscript argues for that result; its relation to this problem is specified below.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
Manuscript 1 (family 039, 2026-10-05): Formal substitutions replace the analytic degeneration used in the complex companions. A nodal equation with two distinct branches even in characteristic two permits the graded-support reshaping and finite torus interpolation to proceed over the ground field.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
Manuscript 1 (family 039, 2026-10-05): The problem selects the mathematical statement summarized here, including its stated hypotheses and parameter range. The cited theorem gives a claimed proof of that assertion in full.

\subsection{Formal verification}
For family 039, the scope page documents the following selections. The selected plane-curve inequality allows unequal multiplicities and repeated components at every allowed point count. A separate statement gives eventual maximality on each polarized complex surface, with a surface-dependent threshold; the higher-dimensional and positive-characteristic companions are not selected here. Manuscript 1 is not among the papers selected by that page, so the family link does not formalize its main conclusion.

This site has not executed the Lean files or checked their dependencies. These descriptions report the scope of the linked declarations, rather than a new verification of the proofs.

\subsection{Status caveat}
OpenAI attributes these results to an internal model. Its release notice cautions that results lacking full formalization can contain mistakes. This site has not independently assessed the proofs; a solved label records the scope of the reported claim.

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item OpenAI, \emph{Maximal multipoint Seshadri constants in positive characteristic}, 2026-10-05; citation key \texttt{OAI:Maximal-multipoint-Seshadri-constants-in-positive-characteristic-October-5-2026}. \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/Maximal-multipoint-Seshadri-constants-in-positive-characteristic-October-5-2026/seshadri-positive-characteristic.pdf}{PDF (GitHub)}; \href{https://github.com/openai/math/raw/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/Maximal-multipoint-Seshadri-constants-in-positive-characteristic-October-5-2026/seshadri-positive-characteristic.pdf}{PDF (direct)}; \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/Maximal-multipoint-Seshadri-constants-in-positive-characteristic-October-5-2026/README.md}{Manuscript page and citation}; \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/main/preprints/Maximal-multipoint-Seshadri-constants-in-positive-characteristic-October-5-2026/seshadri-positive-characteristic.pdf}{Latest version}.
\item Family 039: \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/lean/docs/039.md}{Lean scope}.
